    "rejected": [
      "thm:residual-state-complexity"
    ],
    "note": "Reject: H is exactly the retained query-context set and need not contain the factual context. Hence A_i(v) may be empty, so deleting a fixed nonempty factual block and obtaining Bell(h-1) states is invalid. A two-context binary example already has two reachable/distinguishable partitions while Bell(1)=1. The lower-bound construction is sound only for systems where the factual context is explicitly included, and the runtime improvement therefore does not follow under the current definitions.",
